_pdbx_database_remark.id     700 
_pdbx_database_remark.text   
;SHEET
EACH OF THE TWO CRYSTALLOGRAPHICALLY INDEPENDENT MOLECULES
HAS FIVE BETA STRANS A, B, C, D, E ARRANGED INTO TWO BETA
SHEETS A,B AND C,D,E.
THE TWO MOLECULES ARE LINKED VIA FOUR MAIN-CHAIN HYDROGEN BONDS
BETWEEN LEU52, CYS54, AND GLU56 ON EACH MOLECULE, WITH A
PSEUDO TWO-FOLD AXIS RELATING THE TWO MOLECULES PASSING BETWEEN
THE TWO HYDROGEN BONDS LINING CYS54 ON EACH MOLECULE.
THESE FOUR HYDROGEN BONDS LEAD TO AN EXTENDED SIX-CHAIN BETA
SHEET IN THE DIMER.
;
